WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.402
-My first guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.969
who stars in the new movie,
"Our Friend,"

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.573
which is in theaters
and On Demand this Friday.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.375
Here she is, Dakota Johnson!

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.610
Hi, Dakota!
-Hi.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.013
-Thank you so much
for being on the show.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.682
-Thanks for having me.
-You look great.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.317
I haven't seen you in a while,
so we have a lot to catch up on.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.587
First things first,
last March you gave a tour

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:25.792
to "Architectural Digest,"
and the Internet loved it.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.493
I loved it, too.
It was just --

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:30.029
People were fascinated
with your green kitchen

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.399
and your love of limes.
-Yes.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.168
-During the tour,

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.603
you very clearly state
that you love limes.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.105
Take a look at this video.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.408
-I love limes.
I love them.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:46.479
-Yeah. Now what do you do
with all those limes?

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.982
-I actually didn't even know
that they were in there.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.916
I was giving the tour
and went into the kitchen,

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:53.486
and it was set dressing.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.454
I'm actually --
I'm allergic to limes.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.389
-Oh, my --
Stop it, now.

00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:00.293
-[ Chuckles ]
Yeah, I'm mildly allergic.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:04.163
And honeydew melon, so another
green thing from the outside.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.197
-You're good
with the honeydew melon.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.500
-Oh, no, and the inside.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.602
[ Both laugh ]
-You can't just --

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.305
No one eats the outside
of a honeydew melon.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.840
-It's kind of beige,
and then the inside is green.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.042
-Yes. Correct.
Yes.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.910
I wouldn't eat the outside.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.579
-It makes my tongue itch.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.848
-But limes do the same thing?

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:25.218
-Um, kind of.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.353
Limes make my tongue itch,
too, yeah.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.722
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.523
-That's so bizarre.
I mean, you had a lot of --

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:33.826
So, it was just set dressing,
and it looked pretty,

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.094
and then you were like,
"Yeah, I love limes."

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.997
You're just talking,
going with the flow.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:41.100
-Yeah, because
it was hard to just ignore them,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.702
so I just lied.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:45.872
Just lied.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.139
I went the full
opposite direction.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.409
-Unbelievable.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.311
I'm glad you came clean, man.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.714
-I know that you've also been
working on projects.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.549
Your production company,
TeaTime Pictures, I love that.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:01:59.452
How's it going?

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.187
-TeaTime is going really well.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:05.124
We are actually
gonna shoot our first movie

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.727
that we're producing,
starting February 1st.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:11.130
And Tig Notaro, who you love,
and who I love...

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.833
-I love Tig!
-...and Stephanie Allynne --

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.102
they are married --
are directing together.

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:18.438
-No way!

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.240
Oh, I love them.
What's it called?

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.209
-We're in a very heated debate
about the title at the moment,

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:27.914
so it has no title.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.215
-"Lime Time"
or "Honeydew"?

00:02:30.215 --> 00:02:32.685
-"Honeydew" is not bad.
I would watch that movie.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.654
-I'd see "Honeydew."
-I'd see "Honeydew."

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:37.657
Has nothing to do
with the movie.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.592
-Yeah, no, I'd have
to read the script first.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:44.230
But I'm sure Tig will --
She'll have a good title.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.367
-Yeah, I'm excited.
It's gonna be fun and funny.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.402
And it's, like,
really contained and short

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:53.640
and in L.A., and it'll be --
it'll be cool.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.741
And then we make these lists
every month --

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.910
Well, now,
we used to do it weekly of,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.880
like, top 10 lists
of what's the best to watch,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.649
because I get --
I don't know about you,

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:06.085
but I get really overwhelmed
with kind of content overload

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.954
of like "What --
What am I supposed to watch

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:11.724
on all of the platforms
with all of the amazing shows?"

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.826
-There's too many good shows.
-We kind of comb through them.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:17.229
-And then, I also heard that
you're into music playlists.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.899
What do you make playlists for?

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.602
-Everything.
I make them for, like,

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:28.174
certain times of the year
or certain moods

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:31.944
or road trips or dinner parties.
-Yeah, dinner parties.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.680
-Movies -- I do it a lot
for characters and things.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.148
-Like, if you and I
were to go on a road trip,

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:39.318
what kind of music
would you put on for us?

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.520
-Well, what's the vibe
in our car?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.489
-Fun, hittin' the road.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:47.260
You're driving.
Um...

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.329
-I'm driving?
-I think so, yeah.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:53.265
Do you want
to be passenger seat?

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:56.502
-Well, are we, like --
Is it, like, high energy?

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.738
Does it have an arc?
Does it go, like,

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.572
we start out, maybe we do --

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:04.710
Maybe it starts with
"By Your Side," by Sade,

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.547
because I'm sitting next to you,
by your side, in the car.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.882
And then we're kind of groovin'.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:14.654
And then, maybe it gets
really upbeat halfway through,

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.589
because we're bored,
and it's a road trip.

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:19.459
-I could see us --
-And then we get in a fight.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.428
And then it goes
to, like, Philip Glass.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.862
-Yep.
We get in a little tiff.

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:26.265
-Rolling hills.
-We get in a tiff.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.267
But then we have
to go, like, to the restroom.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:32.138
We get a snack,
get our blood sugar back up.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.675
And then we make up again.
-Yeah, when we stop for a snack

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.677
and you go to the restroom,
then it's,

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:41.313
"Waiting on a Friend,"
by the Stones.

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:42.982
-I was thinking at one point,
do we sing

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.284
"Hit the Road, Jack"
and really get into it

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:48.053
and, like, fake lip-sync
and, like, laugh and stuff?

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.223
Wait.
Now I'm driving.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.057
-Oh, yeah, well...

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.793
-Don't worry about it.
I'll drive.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.194
-That's what the fight was,

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:58.231
because you're a back-seat
driver so then you take over.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.399
'Cause I don't like fighting.
-No, I don't like fighting,

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.001
but, you know, I'm not even
a back-seat driver,

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:06.139
but it's either go with the GPS
or don't go with the GPS.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.975
I can't be watching
you going like, "What?

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.576
What do you mean make a right?
I would never make a right."

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.646
I go, "Yeah, then turn it off."
Just go your way.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.081
-Got it. Got it.
But if we go like --

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.549
♪ Hit the road, Jack,
and don't you come back ♪

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.585
-Where are we going?
-Then you go like...

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.454
♪ That's right ♪
It's like that.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:24.823
And we start choreographing
a thing to it.

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.527
Maybe you have a kerchief.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:30.463
-Probably, yeah,
'cause we're in a convertible.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.498
-Now we're talking.
-Yeah.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.300
-You know we're definitely
in a convertible.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.569
-Where are we going?
-I think we're just touring,

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:41.340
like, those weird things that
you can see, like, on Route 66,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.778
like, World's Biggest Ball
of Yarn, stuff like that.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.012
-Okay, yeah.

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:49.915
-Just for like for some
Instagram photos to post.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:52.918
-My kind of road.
-This sounds fun.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:55.921
I like starting with Sade,
by the way, that's my jam.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:58.123
"By Your Side."
That's my one.

00:05:58.123 --> 00:06:00.727
-Great song.
-Oh, God, right now --

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:03.162
-I'll make you a playlist.
-You will?

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.030
-Yeah.
-I'd love one.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.966
Hey, I want to talk about
your new movie.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.501
-Okay.
-It's called "Our Friend."

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.270
-Yeah.
-It's based on a true story.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.506
For anyone who doesn't know it,
can you set it up?

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:20.412
-Yes. It's based on a true story
of a couple who, the wife --

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:23.415
the woman has terminal cancer.

00:06:23.415 --> 00:06:27.353
And their best friend moves in
and sort of takes care of them.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:33.326
And throughout this, this story,
like tumbling over the years,

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.694
it's about, like,
immense friendship

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:39.098
and pain and torture
and, like, tragedy,

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.968
but also humor and levity
and love

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.938
and most of all just compassion.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.940
-You do a great job
in the movie.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.042
We even get to hear
you sing a little bit.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.611
I don't think we've heard
you sing before, right?

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.981
How was that experience?
-No.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:57.817
That was so scary.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:01.454
I actually had -- I have a
little bit of stage fright.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:03.789
Like, I --
When I come on your show,

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:05.758
I get really nervous,

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.960
and I laugh and then cry
most of the time.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.095
-[ Laughs ]
You've cried.

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:11.797
Yeah, you've cried
a couple times, yes.

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.332
-I've cried a couple times,
which that's fine.

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:16.468
I'm used to it by now,
but singing in front of people

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:19.405
is actually
so terrifying for me.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.940
And we had to shoot the scene
where you don't even

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:25.210
really see me, the camera's,
like, in the back of a --

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.312
like, you can't even really tell
what's going on,

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:30.883
and I was meant to be performing
in, like, community theater.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.786
And they hit playback
of my voice --

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:38.457
my vocal recording
and called "action," and my --

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:43.195
it was like I had a panic attack
that manifested in all the ways

00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:45.464
that it does, that it can,

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:47.833
so, like,
I just took off running.

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:51.170
Running, like around the
theater, around backstage.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.539
I was running around,
and then just started

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:56.308
laughing hysterically,
and everyone on the crew's like,

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:58.477
"What's she doing?"

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:02.114
Running around, laughing,
and then just stopped moving

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.749
and started crying.
-Yeah.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.617
Just complete --
Just embarrassment?

00:08:05.617 --> 00:08:08.521
Or you spun yourself out?

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:13.626
-I just, like, got --
I don't know.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.329
It took over.
I got so scared.

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:19.898
It was like extreme flight mode.

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:22.334
-Gosh.
For the scene --

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.036
Were you doing something
from a play, right?

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:27.306
Was it "Checkers" or something?
-Yes.

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:30.442
-That was the scene?
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:32.644
-Yeah, you know that really
famous musical, "Checkers"?

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:35.580
-Yeah, of course,
the famous musical, "Checkers."

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.118
But that was --
Ah, come on, that was so fun.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.220
Well, you're great in it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.756
Here's Dakota Johnson
in "Our Friend."

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:45.991
Take a look.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:49.395
-I'd like to be blonde.

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:51.296
No, I, um...

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:53.666
I want to have blue hair.
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.601
And I also want
to go to New York one last time

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.369
and see "Les Mis."

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.939
And, um...

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:03.342
Mardi Gras.
I want to be a grand marshal.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.611
And, um...

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:08.580
I want to sing on stage
with Katy Perry.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.682
-Dakota Johnson.
"Our Friend" is in theaters

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:12.184
and On Demand this Friday.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:14.519
When we come back,
Dakota is going to settle

00:09:14.519 --> 00:09:17.189
some of the biggest debates
of all time.

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:19.191
Stick around.

